`cdec.v` shows the suspected issue: `imm_lui` currently concatenates `cinstr[6:2]` directly under the sign fill. Per RV32C, `C.LUI` forms a U-immediate from `{nzimm[17], nzimm[16:12]}` shifted into bits 17:12, so the low 12 bits of the U-immediate are zero; this implementation can shift the field one bit too high. I’m still going to capture the live `cinstr`/expanded value before changing it.
