The next parser failure is from over-propagating taint through `SLTI`: Spike writes boolean `0`, but the parser subtracted `0x1000`. I’m tightening taint propagation to affine PC-derived operations only (`AUIPC`, `ADDI`-style propagation, links), not compares, shifts, logical ops, or arbitrary ALU results.
