The next mismatch is still normalization, not RTL: `sll s10,s9,a2` with shift amount zero preserves the AUIPC-derived value, but a taint-only parser cannot know that without evaluating the operation. The cleaner fix is to remove the PC-base mismatch at the source by linking/running the riscv-dv firmware at PC 0, matching the DUT memory map, instead of normalizing arbitrary writebacks after the fact. I’m testing that path before making it permanent.
