codex
The idx 458 stop is another parser evaluator bug, not hardware: raw Spike logs `x4 0xfffffff3`, matching the DUT, but the evaluator had computed a prior signed `REM` with Python’s modulo sign convention. I’m fixing RV32 `DIV/REM` to use RISC-V trunc-toward-zero and dividend-signed remainder.
apply patch
