Key outcome: this was not an RTL `cdec.v` bug and not a fetch bug. The raw cdec input was `cinstr=6db5`, expanded to `0000ddb7`, and raw Spike wrote `0x0000d000`. The false `0x0000c000` came from the Spike commit parser’s broad PC-base writeback normalization.

Fix was in [spike_commit.py](/home/edauser/project/SOC/Magpie_M1/flow/v2_pipeline/lib/spike_commit.py), plus regression tests and honest J8 bounded-rerun reporting. No RTL changed.

